// Sophisticated Backpacks' Pump upgrade keeps water quality: water collected from the world is graded
// where it lies, and buckets in the hand are emptied into and filled from the tank with their grade.
// Only nodes that set deps.sophisticated_core have it on the runClient classpath.
//
// Every backpack is a gold backpack from tools/agent/integrations/sophisticated/sophisticated-pack with a Tank and a Pump upgrade.
// Sophisticated only unpacks a template the first time the backpack is opened, so each is opened with
// the real right click and closed again. Read the exports under the world's
// datapacks/thirstout_backpack_templates, and the replies named below:
// - pump_world_plains: a one-block pool in a plains biome is pumped into the tank. "plainsBottle" is a
//   bottle filled from the same pool by hand first; the tank has to hold 1000 mB with that same
//   water_purity.
// - pump_world_ocean: the same pool with its biome set to ocean: the tank holds water_salty.
// - pump_world_filter: the plains pool again, with the pump's filter set to plain water. A filter set to
//   water takes water of any grade, so the tank holds the plains grade as in the first case. Without the
//   integration's filter rule it would stay empty.
// - pump_block_out and pump_block_in: the same through a Create Fluid Tank next to the player, the
//   pump's "fluid handlers" setting. Create is on this node's runClient classpath. A block entity is not
//   readable from server.command, which runs off the server thread, so these ask with client.command and
//   the answer is the "[CHAT]" line in the client's log: pump_block_out has to leave the Create tank with
//   1000 mB of water_purity 3 ("Test passed"), and pump_block_in has to empty a Create tank of purity-0
//   water into the backpack, whose export then holds water_purity 0.
// - pump_hand_skin: 1000 mB of purity 3 pumped into an empty waterskin in the off hand: "handSkinFilled"
//   passes, the skin holding three servings, and 250 mB stays in the tank.
// - pump_hand_in: a purity-0 bucket in the off hand is poured in. "handInEmptied" passes, and the tank
//   holds 1000 mB with water_purity 0.
// - pump_hand_out: 1000 mB of purity-3 water is pumped into an empty bucket in the off hand.
//   "handOutFilled" passes, and the tank is empty. Without the integration the bucket stays empty: the
//   pump asks for plain water and the backpack only hands out water whose components match.
//
// SophisticatedAgent is a throwaway world: copy level.dat out of any 1.21.1 world (its player keeps
// their effects, so the script clears them: a Farmer's Delight world leaves Nourishment behind) into
// run/1.21.1-neoforge/saves/SophisticatedAgent, and tools/agent/integrations/sophisticated/sophisticated-pack into its datapacks
// folder, fresh for each run. Then:
//     ./gradlew ":1.21.1-neoforge:runClient" -Pagent=tools/agent/integrations/sophisticated/sophisticated-pump.jsonl -Pquickplay=SophisticatedAgent

